{
  "_provenance": "Stufe3/Dokumentenaustausch/DocumentReference-Read.feature: 'Beziehung zu anderen Dokumenten: Dieses Dokument ersetzt ein (beliebiges) Dokument' - the assertion relatesTo.where(code = 'replaces' and target.reference.exists()).exists() requires DocumentReference-Read-Example to point at a replaced document. The prose leaves that document's identity free ('beliebig') and no data key names it, so it is absent from the inventory. Seeded so the reference resolves: the suite never reads it, but a dangling target would make the seed set internally inconsistent and would fail on any endpoint enforcing referential integrity on write. Authored to ISiKDokumentenMetadaten anyway - not because the suite asks, but because a superseded pathology report in a real system is itself a document with metadata, and IRIS $validate then checks our own authoring rather than waving it through as a bare DocumentReference.",
